Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.clips,{"tom|You took the train to meet the plane.":"","tnb|I took the train to meet the man. The plane was a bonus.":"","tnb|Look who flew in for my big day. I am on a forty-minute lunch. I spent thirty of it on the Metro.":"","tom|Then we get Nara. Then I watch you be very important.":"","tnb|Big shoot today. BACKLOT BEDLAM. Car chases, a saloon, a fake New York. I have forty costumes on one rack, and every single one is steamed.":"","tnb|Also, Olivia dropped Nara at your place again. Family trip to the desert. She has been howling at your front door since nine.":"","tnb|Very, very important. I have a lanyard.":"","tnb|She is coming to set. I already asked. Nobody said yes, but nobody said no fast enough.":"","tom|Hi. Hi. Yes. I know. I was gone FOREVER. It was six days.":"","moss|Sunset Gold Studios. Closed set. Name?":"","tnb|Ray, it is me. Wardrobe. I left eighty minutes ago. You waved.":"","moss|I wave at everybody. That is the job. Go on in.":"","dot|TNB! TNB! The rack! Rack two! It is GONE.":"","tnb|Gone? It is a rack. It has wheels. It does not have ambitions.":"","dot|It was right there in Stage 7. Then the fog machine turned itself on, and the lights went out, and things started CLAPPING.":"","la_woman|Dana Park. Director. First feature. Without wardrobe there is no shoot. Without a shoot there is no movie.":"","tom|Friction Sprites. On a closed set.":"","la_woman|And the Backlot is full of little grumpy things. One of them ate a cue card. One of them is clapping at the horse.":"","tnb|Babe. Forty costumes. I steamed every single one. By hand. While humming.":"","tom|Then we go get them back. Nara, stay close. This is a professional environment.":"","tnb|She has never eaten anything that fast. Not even my shoe.":"","bun|Here. For the road. Do not tell the grips.":"","bun|Plain roast chicken. No salt, no skin, no sauce. I keep it for the grips. They are also picky.":"","tom|Nara. NARA. Do not...":"","tnb|That is a closed set! She is not on the call sheet!":"","tnb|The Backlot. Main Street up on the left, the Western street on the right, New York down on the left. All fake. All very expensive.":"","tnb|She peed on the hydrant. That hydrant is fiberglass. That hydrant is a PROP.":"","tom|She does not know that. Let her have this.":"","tom|Good girl. Professional environment, very good girl.":"","tnb|That is a costume tag. That is MY tag. WARDROBE, RACK 2, HAND WASH ONLY. I underlined it twice.":"","tnb|And it smells like fog juice. The grape kind. Only Stage 7 has a fog machine.":"","tom|Then we clear the sets. One at a time. Main Street, the Western street, New York.":"","tnb|Stage 7 is locked from the inside, though. And every set out here has a Sprite on it wrecking the shoot. The crew cannot work like this.":"","grump|Pinch. This is MY set. I hold up the lines. Every line. I hold up this one: GO AWAY.":"","tnb|Those are the neatest cue cards I have ever seen. Is that calligraphy?":"","tnb|Cut. Reset. Back to one. Everybody gets a touch-up.":"","grump|...Do not try to be nice to me. Nobody is nice to me. I will PINCH.":"","tnb|Main Street is clear. The bank is safe. The pie is still foam.":"","tnb|All three sets are clear. And Stage 7 just opened. That is where the fog came from.":"","dot|(on the radio) ...kkkt... Stage 7! The big door just unlocked itself! From the INSIDE! Is that bad? That feels bad.":"","tom|It is very fast. And very loud.":"","tnb|That is every clapper I have ever met.":"","toad|SNAP! Scene one, take one! SNAP! I go first! Nothing happens until I clap! SNAP!":"","tom|The Western street is clear. The horse can come out of its trailer now.":"","tnb|Watch the screech, babe. It shuts you right up. No skills.":"","skeeter|Bzzz. I hear everything on this set. Everything. Your knees click, Tom.":"","tnb|New York is clear. It never looked better. It is plywood.":"","tom|The stage set is at the top. The rack is up there. I can smell the steamer.":"","tnb|Somebody killed the work lights. And look, the catwalk is up. You only raise a catwalk when you are hiding something up there.":"","tnb|The main light rig runs the catwalk motor. If I get power back to it, the catwalk comes down.":"","tnb|Three junction boxes. They have to come up in the right order or the dimmer pops. The rig will tell us the order.":"","tom|You fixed a whole soundstage with tape.":"","tnb|Blue, amber, red. And one strip of gaffer tape. Okay, two. Okay, four.":"","tnb|I fix everything with tape. You know this. Your kitchen drawer knows this.":"","tnb|My rack. MY RACK. All forty. Still steamed. Oh, I could cry.":"","tom|You took the rack.":"","bigone|CUT! CUT! CUT! Who said you could walk onto my set? The blocking is WRONG.":"","bigone|Forty years I have been on this lot. Forty years of bad takes, yelled through ME. Nobody ever gets it right.":"","tnb|Babe. It is a megaphone in a beret. It has notes.":"","tom|This is a closed set. And you are not on the call sheet.":"","bigone|If there are no costumes, there is no take. If there is no take, there is no BAD take. It is perfect. It is my best work.":"","tnb|Back to one, everybody. Touch-ups.":"","tnb|Forty. I counted. I am going to count again. Forty.":"","tnb|Babe, when it says CUT, put WARDROBE on whoever is next. When it braces, Popcorn Jump. Or just tell it GREAT TAKE. Three times.":"","bigone|Fine. FINE. That’s a wrap. On me. I am going back in the prop closet.":"","tnb|And look. Somebody stuck a note on the steamer. \"Paid in full.\" With a gold coin taped to it.":"","tom|A gold coin. Again. Somebody keeps leaving these around. Somebody in a long coat, if Oolong’s kettle is right.":"","tnb|Spooky. I love it. I hate it. Help me push. This thing has four wheels and four opinions.":"","la_woman|The rack! The costumes! We can shoot! We are shooting! That is a WRAP on today, everybody!":"","dot|WRAP PARTY AT CRAFTY! Toni made a cake! It is shaped like a clapper! It is not clapping!":"","la_woman|TNB, the studio wants you to have this. Gold-plated. It is the steamer from the lot’s very first wardrobe department.":"","tnb|You know what this whole day was? A real steam-ulating experience.":"","tnb|I am going to cry. I am not going to cry. I am a professional. I am crying a little.":"","la_woman|And crew jackets. Wrap Party Jackets. Only the crew gets one. You are crew now. Even the dog.":"","tom|...":"","tnb|Worth it?":"","tom|I flew three thousand miles for that pun.":"","tnb|You are the only uncle.":"","tom|Worth it. But for the record? That was a CLOSED set!":"","tom|Which makes me the good one. By default. I will take it.":"","tom|A text from Amy. \"Parent-teacher conference night is Thursday. Thirty parents. I need backup. Bring snacks. And bring the good uncle.\"":"","moss|Good job, Tom. Do not tell anyone I said good job.":"","moss|Nobody came through my gate. Nobody with legs.":"","moss|Ray here. Shoot wrapped. Nobody got past me. Except the megaphone. And the moths. And the dog.":"","moss|Tom. Plus one dog. Plus one boyfriend who already works here. Fine. Go on in.":"","moss|Little things, though. Buzzing. Clapping. One of them asked me for a compliment. I said no. I regret it.":"","moss|Nobody gets past Ray. Except the dog. The dog got past Ray. Do not tell anyone.":"","bun|Craft services! Take a bagel. Take two. Nobody is counting. I am counting.":"","bun|The crew eats like a swarm of locusts. Polite locusts. With lanyards.":"","dot|We WRAPPED! On time! Well. Four hours late. Which is on time for us.":"","dot|I am going to sleep for a week. In my car. With the headset on.":"","dot|Rack two is still missing. Forty costumes. The actors are filming in bathrobes.":"","dot|Last thing on my radio before the static was the Stage 7 fog machine. It turned itself on.":"","dot|Kiki. Production assistant. I have a headset, three radios and zero answers.":"","dot|If anybody asks, I am walking somewhere important. I am always walking somewhere important.":"","la_woman|We got the shot. All of them. Even the one with the horse.":"","la_woman|Without wardrobe there is no shoot. Without a shoot there is no movie.":"","la_woman|Tell TNB the costumes looked incredible. Tell him I said incredible. Tell him twice.":"","la_woman|Without a movie I go back to directing car commercials. I love cars. I do not love talking cars.":"","la_woman|Dana Park. Director. First feature. Please do not ask me how it is going.":"","grump|I have been an extra in forty movies. You have seen the back of my head forty times.":"","grump|They said there would be a hot lunch. It was a cold sandwich.":"","grump|I am back. They reset the scene.":"","grump|Round 2. I got a new coat. Same coat, actually.":"","grump|Round 3. I got a new coat. Same coat, actually.":"","grump|Round 4. I got a new coat. Same coat, actually.":"","grump|...Nine hours in holding. Nine.":"","grump|Round 5. I got a new coat. Same coat, actually.":"","grump|I am Man in Coat Number Four. They never call Number Four.":"","skeeter|Every time someone says CUT, I am the last to know.":"","skeeter|Bzzz. I am back in frame.":"","skeeter|I hang over everybody all day. Nobody looks up. Nobody says thank you.":"","skeeter|Round 2. I can hear you breathing.":"","skeeter|Round 3. I can hear you breathing.":"","skeeter|Round 4. I can hear you breathing.":"","skeeter|Round 5. I can hear you breathing.":"","skeeter|...Fuzz. I am fuzzy. Leave me alone.":"","skeeter|I hear everything. EVERYTHING. It is a lot.":"","toad|Take two! Snap!":"","toad|Every take starts with me and nobody remembers me.":"","toad|SNAP. I go first. I ALWAYS go first. Nothing happens until I clap.":"","toad|Round 2. Rolling. Speed. SNAP.":"","toad|Round 3. Rolling. Speed. SNAP.":"","toad|Round 4. Rolling. Speed. SNAP.":"","toad|Round 5. Rolling. Speed. SNAP.":"","toad|...Snap. I am resting between takes.":"","toad|Scene four, take nine. Do not ask about the other eight.":"","mudling|Back again. Thicker.":"","mudling|They pump me in and then they open the doors. Every time.":"","mudling|Everything looks better in fog. Mysterious. Soft. Nobody can see anybody.":"","mudling|Round 3. Can you see me? No. Good.":"","mudling|Round 2. Can you see me? No. Good.":"","mudling|Round 4. Can you see me? No. Good.":"","mudling|...Hazy. I am feeling hazy.":"","mudling|Round 5. Can you see me? No. Good.":"","mudling|Do not look at me. You cannot see me anyway.":"","grump|Pinch. I wrote that one myself.":"","grump|New cards. Same feelings.":"","grump|I hold up the lines. Every line. Nobody ever says \"nice handwriting.\"":"","grump|Round 2. This card says ROUND 2.":"","grump|Round 3. This card says ROUND 3.":"","grump|Round 4. This card says ROUND 4.":"","grump|Round 5. This card says ROUND 5.":"","grump|...I am rewriting my cards.":"","grump|Nobody reads my cards. They read the actors.":"","bigone|From the top!":"","bigone|CUT! CUT! Again! The light was wrong! The FEELING was wrong!":"","bigone|Forty years of bad takes. I have heard every one of them. Through me.":"","bigone|Round 2. Take 2. Still wrong.":"","bigone|Round 3. Take 3. Still wrong.":"","bigone|Round 4. Take 4. Still wrong.":"","bigone|Round 5. Take 5. Still wrong.":"","bigone|Nobody gets it right. NOBODY.":"","bigone|...From the top. Again. Always from the top.":"","sal|The studio lot is at the east end of the boulevard. Big gate. Grumpy guard.":"","sal|Airport? You JUST landed. Your young man is on a shoot. Go watch him be important.":""});
Object.assign(DIALOG_CLIPS.voices,{"tnb":{"voice_id":"QPmHuIriDGOvu1d9U7wn","name":"SuperDale - a mid-age voice & Friendly  (male, middle_aged, us midwest, informative_educational)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"tom":{"voice_id":"cjVigY5qzO86Huf0OWal","name":"Eric - Smooth, Trustworthy","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.85},"direction":"","designed":false},"moss":{"voice_id":"7vp7iK3I8DiDLgC90c3t","name":"AoT Moss","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A tall, gentle man in his thirties with a deep, slow, mellow American voice. Dreamy and laid back, long pauses, quietly pleased with his own puns. Warm low tone. Clean studio recording."},"dot":{"voice_id":"gYzudf4C0nXnEecqXK5t","name":"AoT Dot","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small woman in her forties with a quick, crisp, precise American voice, slightly nasal. Talks fast in short exact phrases like she is reading a tally sheet. Proud of her accuracy. Clean studio recording."},"la_woman":{"voice_id":"eLXwnyHT9UJHbuyheJ9m","name":"AoT LA neighbor (woman)","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her early thirties with a relaxed, warm, slightly husky Los Angeles voice. Easygoing, wry, a little tired, friendly neighbor energy. Clean studio recording."},"bun":{"voice_id":"FSFvvh3OTPle9DfVJIu3","name":"AoT Bun","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A woman in her thirties with a bubbly, warm, bright American voice. Friendly shop greeter energy, smiling while she talks, loves a bread pun. Clean studio recording."},"grump":{"voice_id":"moX2FuSiiLmOw0uEq4OU","name":"AoT Pond Grump","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A grumpy cartoon swamp creature, low gravelly grumbling voice, cranky and wet-sounding, easily offended, a big softie underneath. Animated character voice."},"toad":{"voice_id":"jcb48kKcDpNXjAxnAP2c","name":"AoT Bog Toad","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A huge cartoon toad, deep croaky throaty voice with a rumbling ribbit, territorial and proud, a bit vain. Animated character voice."},"skeeter":{"voice_id":"3NkCp1SubvPIw3g0s7Rf","name":"AoT Skeeter Swarm","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A cartoon swarm of mosquitoes speaking as one, high-pitched, thin, whiny and buzzy voice with a nasal zzz on every s, nosy and impatient. Animated character voice."},"bigone":{"voice_id":"qDteMRfOWoUEc7kcfWvl","name":"AoT The Big One","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"An enormous ancient cartoon pond fish, huge slow booming bass voice with gurgling bubbles, pompous and boastful but childlike and easily delighted underneath. Animated character voice."},"mudling":{"voice_id":"E2hOWZ8x3nGJuQURP3SG","name":"AoT Mudling","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A small, silly cartoon creature made of mud, gloopy gurgling voice with wet bubbly consonants, slow and sulky, childlike and a little sad. Animated character voice."},"sal":{"voice_id":"gcJ5PkVgShIxtP5HgbZK","name":"AoT Sal","model":"eleven_v4","settings":{"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.8},"direction":"","designed":true,"desc":"A man in his fifties with a thick Long Island New York accent, a slightly nasal, raspy, fast and friendly voice. Chatty taxi driver, warm and a little dramatic, proud of his one cab. Clean studio recording."}});
